Under <a href="#sp:poincare" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="sp:poincare">[sp:poincare]</a>, there are smooth functions $u_N$ on $U$, for all sufficiently large integers $N$, such that $$\label{sp:potential-bounds}
 u_N\le0,\qquad \mathrm d\mathrm d^cu_N\ge-\omega,
 \qquad \|u_N\|_2\le C N^n.$$ For every compact set $K\subset U$, there are $c_K>0$ and $N_K$ with $$\label{sp:potential-depth}
 \sup_Ku_N\le-c_KN\qquad(N\ge N_K).$$ For each fixed $N$, the function $u_N$ belongs to every $H^k$ and has bounded derivatives of all orders.

There are $C,\epsilon>0$, independent of $N,a,g$, such that $$\label{sp:cell-count}
 \#\{g\in P:A_a(g)\ge1\}\le C N^{2n},$$ and $$\label{sp:cell-exponential}
 \int_{gL}\exp\!\left(
       \frac{-\epsilon u_N(a^{-1}x)}{A_a(g)+1}\right)\omega^n\le C.$$ For each $R<\infty$ there is $C_R$ such that $$\label{sp:cell-neighbors}
 C_R^{-1}(A_a(g)+1)\le A_a(h)+1\le C_R(A_a(g)+1)$$ whenever the distance between $gL$ and $hL$ is at most $R$.

Suppose a smooth positive multiplier $h$ on $E^*$ satisfies $$\label{sp:weight-hypotheses}
 1\le h\le e^b,
 \qquad \mathrm i\Theta_{E^*,h}\ge-C_0t\Omega_S,
 \qquad b,t\ge0.$$ Then the complete $\bar\partial$ complex of $E$-valued $(0,*)$-forms with multiplier $k=h^{-1}$ is exact with closed ranges. Every closed form $F$ in this complex has a solution $\bar\partial v=F$ satisfying $$\label{sp:weighted-solution}
 \|v\|_{S,k}\le
 C\bigl(e^{b/4}+\sqrt t\,e^{b/2}\bigr)\|F\|_{S,k}.$$ The constant depends on $M$, $C_0$ and $\delta$, but not on $S,b,t$.
